/*Some minor spoilers may be lurking in the following . . .*/

Shields of reflection are lauded highly in this group, but amulets of 
reflection are hardly mentioned.  Why?  I mean, I know an amulet of life-
saving is what you're supposed to be wearing around your neck, but I find
that being able to wield the Tsurugi and have reflection at the same time
is highly useful.

My Level 13 Elf has amulets of reflection, ESP, and magic-breathing which 
get switched on a regular basis depending on the situation (especially
since I have neither SoR, means of getting over water, or a helm of
ESP).  I scout around using the ESP and then get on the reflection when
I see baddies a'comin'.  And the magic-breathing came in handy when I
encountered eel rooms for the first time, and when sneaking around the
back of the castle.  (had to cast levitation to get over the trapdoors, tho)

BTW, when slaughtering trolls or playing with black puddings, it is very
useful to have a tinning kit on hand.  That way the T's won't reappear and
the P's won't rot before you can eat them all, and you won't be tempted
to choke yourself to death on the buggers.  And, eating tinned P's won't
give you stomach acid.  (a blessed tinning kit is especially useful).



